dialogue.mmo_sawyer.first_words.text = Hm. Calluses on your palms and bark on your boots. You'll do.\nName's Marn. I saw timber. Down here in the <color is="#ffd97a">Forgotten Temple</color> it's all stone and no trees, so a sawyer's a rare thing, and I keep a mill or two for whoever can feed one. Say hello and we'll talk.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.first_words.opt.hail = Hello, Marn.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.menu.text = Marn's still here. Logs don't saw themselves, so say what you need.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.trophy_hail.text = Hold on. Show me that.\nThat's a <color is="#ffd97a">Sawmiller's Hatchet</color>. Mithril, balanced at a mill and nowhere else. I've not seen its like in years, and never in a hand this green.\nThe mill hands one of those out about as often as a log splits itself. Keep it sharp.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.trophy_hail.opt.show = It came out of the mill.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.trophy_talk.text = Still carrying the <color is="#ffd97a">Sawmiller's Hatchet</color>. Good. A blade like that wants working, so don't let it hang on a wall. What do you need?
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.rights_offer.text = I've a <b>Sawmill</b> going spare. I don't hand them to just anybody, mind.\nGo chop <b>timber</b>. Cut <b>planks</b> on a hand bench till you know what a plank costs in sweat, and bring me a share. Do that and the mill's yours.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.rights_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring you planks.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.rights_brief.text = <b>Timber</b> off the tree and <b>planks</b> off a hand bench. That's the job. The hand bench is slow, I know it. That's the point. You'll want the mill all the more for it.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.rights_ready.text = Let's see them. <b>Planks</b>, hand-cut, edges all over the place. Good. You'll not cut another one like that once the mill's running. Hand them over and it's yours.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.rights_ready.opt.turnin = Here are the planks.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.cut_offer.text = Set the <b>Sawmill</b> down somewhere flat. Walk up with <b>logs</b> in hand and use the block, and the mill takes them off you. Use it again and you're sawing.\nRun it a while, mill me some lumber, and bring back a stack of <b>planks</b> so I can see your cut.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.cut_offer.opt.accept = I'll get it running.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.grain_offer.text = Every <b>log</b> has more in it than plain boards. The mill knows the decorative <b>cut</b> and the ornate one too, it only wants telling. Crouch as you use the block and it'll ask which.\nMill me some of each, so I know you can read a grain.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.grain_offer.opt.accept = I'll try every cut.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.bench_offer.text = One mill's a start. It's no yard. Put a proper load of lumber through yours, the kind of load that empties a hillside, and bring me the <b>sap</b> it sweats out while you're at it.\nDo that and I'll find you a second <b>Sawmill</b>.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.bench_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring the sap.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.essence_offer.text = You've the hang of planks. Now the other thing.\nOld <b>wood</b> holds something that isn't sap and isn't bark, and a mill with a good hand on it shakes it loose. <b>Life essence</b>, the alchemists call it. I call it the fat of the log. Mill till you've a load of it, and bring me a share.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.essence_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring you essence.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.essence_offer.opt.what = What's in the wood?
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.essence_ready.text = There it is. <b>Life essence</b>, still warm from the cut. Most sawyers go a lifetime and never spot it in the sawdust. Hand it over.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.essence_ready.opt.turnin = Here's the essence.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.edge_offer.text = Short jobs are done. Now a long one.\nStand at that mill for a shift that'd wear out a lesser back, and get your woodcutting up to where I'd call you a sawyer to your face. Nothing to hand in. Come back when it's done and I'll know.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.edge_offer.opt.accept = I'll put the shift in.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.order_ready.text = The day's order. <b>Planks</b> and <b>bark</b>, counted, stacked square. That's how I like a delivery. Same again tomorrow, if you're up for it.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.order_ready.opt.turnin = Here's today's order.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.ready_generic.text = You've the look of somebody carrying a finished job. Put it down and we'll settle.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.ready_generic.opt.turnin = Here's what I've done.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.active_generic.text = Still on the job, then. The mill won't run without you standing at it. Go on.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.yard_talk.text = Sawyer. That's what I call you now, and I don't say it to many.\nYou've a yard of your own to run. Mine's this corner of the <color is="#ffd97a">Forgotten Temple</color>, and it's enough. Come by when you want to talk wood.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.bench_talk.text = You've a mill now. Keep it fed. Planks come first, and the longer you stand at it the more a log gives up. There's work here when you want it.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.how_it_works.text = <b>Logs</b> in hand, use the block, and the mill takes them off you. Use it again and you're sawing.\nYour <b>hatchet</b> does the cutting, so a better one means more planks a cycle, and more of everything else the mill turns up in a log, bark to essence. Crouch as you use the block and it'll ask which <b>cut</b> you want.\nThat's the whole of it. The rest is standing there.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.how_it_works.opt.wood = What else is in a log?
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.how_it_works.opt.back = Got it.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.what_is_in_wood.text = Bark. Sap. Fibre. Sticks. Every log's got those and the mill throws them off with the sawdust.\nOld wood keeps something else, deeper in, down in the heartwood. The alchemists boil it and call it <b>life essence</b>. I call it the fat of the log. A steady hand and a good hatchet shake it loose. A clumsy one gets sawdust.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.what_is_in_wood.opt.back = Good to know.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.hatchet_tease.text = There's a <color is="#ffd97a">Sawmiller's Hatchet</color>. Mithril, balanced at the mill, keener than anything a forge puts out. Nobody makes it.\nNow and then a mill hands one to a sawyer who's stood at it long enough with a fine blade already in hand. And I mean now and then. I've seen it happen. Not to me.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.hatchet_tease.opt.back = I'll keep sawing.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.opt.returned = I'm back with what you asked for.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.opt.quests = Anything need cutting?
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.opt.how = How does the mill work?
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.opt.edge = Ever seen a better edge?
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.opt.nothing = Nothing for now.
